## Essential Imports
CRITICAL: Always include the correct import statement when using any of these symbols.
Forgetting an import will cause build failures.

- Always `import Combine` when using: @Published, ObservableObject, PassthroughSubject, CurrentValueSubject, AnyCancellable, Cancellable
- Always `import SwiftUI` when using: View, @State, @Binding, @Environment, @StateObject, @ObservedObject, @EnvironmentObject
- Always `import MapKit` when using: MKMapView, MKAnnotation, Map, MapAnnotation
- Always `import CoreLocation` when using: CLLocationManager, CLLocation, CLLocationCoordinate2D
- Always `import Foundation` when using: URL, URLSession, JSONDecoder, JSONEncoder, Data, Date, UUID
- Always `import UIKit` when using: UIViewController, UIView, UIImage, UIColor (iOS UIKit apps only)

## Build & Development
